1. DEFINITIONS

"Software" means the Cerberus source code, executable code, bundled
original artwork, documentation and modifications distributed in a
revision that includes this license, but excludes third-party
components governed by their own licenses.

"Licensor" means the copyright holder(s) authorized to license the
relevant portions of the Software.

"Personal Use" means use by an individual acting solely for their own
noncommercial hobby, learning, experimentation, personal organization
or personal research. Work performed for an employer, client,
organization, business or revenue-generating activity is not Personal
Use, even if the individual uses their own computer.

"Commercial Use" means use of the Software in connection with any
business, paid work, client service, organizational workflow, product,
commercial service, or activity intended to generate revenue, directly
or indirectly. This includes internal business use and use by a
for-profit or nonprofit organization in an operational workflow.

"Heavy Production Use" means ANY of the following, regardless of
whether the use generates revenue:
(a) more than 10,000 newly saved capture items in any rolling 30-day
    period across one person's Cerberus installations;
(b) more than 10 GiB of newly imported attachment data in any rolling
    30-day period across one person's Cerberus installations; or
(c) shared or multi-user deployment, centralized ingestion or an
    unattended data-processing service used by more than one person.
Duplicate captures that do not create a new record do not count
toward (a). A GiB equals 1,073,741,824 bytes.

